| `scripts/check_venv.py` | The shared Python dependency check derives extras from pyproject and the config loader and emits the pip advice preflight reuses. Fails before any gate runs, naming each package and the exact `pip install -e ".[<extras>]"` command, when the venv lacks a requirement of `pyproject.toml`'s core, the gate's extras or an enabled transport's extra, or holds one outside its specifier; the command carries `--index-url <url>` when `install_sources.python_index` names a mirror. | `make check-venv`; imported by preflight | [`venv.extras`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`transports.extras`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`install_sources.python_index`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`PY`](settings.md#make-variables) | Checks distribution metadata, not imports; installs nothing and never reads the network, so it cannot tell a broken install whose metadata is intact. It does not judge a dependency's own unconditional dependencies, which are pip's to resolve. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md), [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
